 "reference": "RMC-BestFit @ c2e6192. Every numeric literal is transcribed verbatim from the upstream Test_*TrendTests.cs files under RMC.BestFit.Tests/Univariate/TrendFunctions (not computed by this port's own C++). `values` in each case's `options.trend` is the explicit parameter vector the toolbox `trend` group's build_spec_trend applies with ITrendModel::set_parameter_values, in the same order the transcribed test sets model.Parameters[i].Value; `start_index` matches the transcribed StartIndex. The GeneralLinear case instead pins the documented type-only-dispatch fallthrough to ConstantTrend (trend_model_factory.hpp; mirrors the C# SetTrendModel if-chain, which has no GeneralLinear branch) rather than a GeneralLinearFunctionTests.cs literal, since GeneralLinearFunction itself needs a covariate matrix this grammar does not carry.",
